#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:2
msgid "gconf interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `gconf`  interface  allows access to any item from the legacy [GConf "
"configuration system](https://gitlab.gnome.org/Archive/gconf) for the "
"current user, typically used by old GNOME desktop libraries and applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"This interface needs to be manually connected because _gconf_ is a global "
"database for GNOME desktop and application settings and offers no "
"application isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:9
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:11
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:13
msgid ""
"Modern applications should use dconf/gsettings instead and this interface is "
"provided for old codebases that cannot be migrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gconf-interface.md:15
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

